driver: a wrapper that keeps its C function's name counts by its anchor

rustc rejects a doc(alias) equal to its item's name, so such a wrapper
carries none, and fn.ffibox.wrapper, which reads aliases, missed it. A fn
named as a -sys fn now counts where its documentation carries that
function's anchor, a doc line of its own in the form ffimap api reads.
The cells fixture holds one such wrapper and two fns named alike that
are none. Proposal: libgit2-crustify's
crustify/evolution/ffimap-wrapper-without-alias.

Co-Authored-By: crustify <crustify@berkeley.edu>


